{"school":{"dbn":"27Q317","name":"Waterside Children's Studio School","boro":"Queens","district":"27","district_label":"District 27","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"PK-5","status":"open","enrollment":436,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"140 Beach 112 Street, Queens, NY 11694","phone":"718-634-1344","website":"HTTPS://WATERSIDECSS.ORG/","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/67949","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"The Waterside Childrens Studio School will be relocated to the Q593 building at 140 Beach 112th Street, Queens, NY, 11694 beginning in the 2023-2024 school year. WCSS MISSION \nAt the Waterside Children\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0099s Studio School, our mission is to inspire a community of life- long learners by nurturing their innovation, creativity and social-emotional well-being in a diverse and inclusive environment. \n\nWCSS VISION \nAt the Waterside Children's Studio School, our vision is to provide a safe and nurturing 21st Century learning environment where creativity and artistic expression are integral to the academic and emotional success of every child. Through music, drama, visual arts, film, technology, writing and dance, our rigorous and progressive curriculum will empower ALL of our children to grow academically, creatively and socially. They will acquire the critical thinking, personal integrity and self-esteem that go beyond the classroom walls. As a community, we will take pride and ownership of our school and celebrate all of our accomplishments.\n This school has ASD Nest: Open to students currently enrolled in the ASD (Autism Spectrum Disorder) Nest program. If you are applying to ASD programs for the first time, please visit www.schools.nyc.gov/specializedprograms for the application and contact ASDprograms@schools.nyc.gov with questions.","start_time":"8:00 AM","end_time":"2:20 PM","languages":nul